  "policy": {
    "accept_selection": "accept at the consumer min_score (default 0.85) after veto; a common dimension-logit offset maximises calibration accept count with at least five accepts and precision at least 0.90; fallback maximises attainable precision and is recorded",
    "check_cutoff": "one cutoff per check, maximising defect recall minus accepted false positive rate with that rate at most 0.10, at least 2 defects caught and separation at least 0.02",
    "check_selection": "five-fold copy-group CV within calibration selects the budget with highest held-out defect recall whose pooled 95% Wilson upper false-veto bound is at most 0.10; ties use the smaller budget; check cutoffs and union are then refitted on calibration. If none qualifies, disable all learned vetoes and retain only the fixed contradiction rule, provided its observed CV rate is at most 0.10; its interval is reported without claiming a bound.",
    "reject_selection": "the interval [min_score - 0.05, min_score) uses chat_review; below it refines. The policy width is one point of a 20-point rubric.",
    "rubric": "mean of four dimension logits normalised to 0..1, reported as 0..20 dimension scores; nonnegative weights on category expectation (best=1, middle=0.5, worst=0) and own-check compliance (1-p_failure). Binary defensibility supervision fits dimension evidence, not dimension gold labels. L2 penalty is selected by five-fold copy-group CV AUC.",
